      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For this boardroom role requiring immense gravitas, Marcus Washington stands out as the top choice due to his proven track record of managing large cross-functional teams and his directly communicative, high-pressure style. James Sterling is a close second, as his Yale MBA background and experience leading high-stakes restructuring projects signal the traditional prestige often valued for Fortune 500 introductions, though his rowing captaincy may be less relevant now. Ultimately, while Arjun Mehta's analytical depth is impressive, he lacks the specific executive presence or boardroom command needed for this specific high-level client-facing objective.",
